Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 01:42:12 -0400
Subject: stop the Space icons jumping when a name appears

Hovering a Space raised its name above the row, and hiding the label when there
was no name took it out of the layout -- so the row moved the moment you hovered
it, and the icon you were pointing at slid out from under the pointer. A click
after a hover landed on nothing.

The label is now always laid out and simply carries no text when there is
nothing to say.

Found by driving the real UI with synthetic mouse events posted to the browser's
own process, which is also how the claim in patch 0019 that "the icons do not
jump" was shown to be wrong. It was true when written and stopped being true
when the label started being hidden.

Why: the switcher was unusable with a mouse, which no screenshot would have
shown.
Removable when: never.
---
 chrome/browser/ui/views/spaces/space_switcher_view.cc | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/spaces/space_switcher_view.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/spaces/space_switcher_view.cc
index 94244e4cc81ab..a7c3d088c5215 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/spaces/space_switcher_view.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/spaces/space_switcher_view.cc
@@ -119,7 +119,9 @@ SpaceSwitcherView::SpaceSwitcherView(SpaceModel& model, Browser& browser)
   auto name = std::make_unique<views::Label>();
   name->SetHorizontalAlignment(gfx::ALIGN_LEFT);
   name->SetPreferredSize(gfx::Size(0, kNameHeight));
-  name->SetVisible(false);
+  // Always laid out, even with nothing to say. Hiding it removes it from the
+  // layout, which moves the icon row -- so the icon being hovered slides out
+  // from under the pointer, and a click after a hover lands on nothing.
   hovered_name_ = AddChildView(std::move(name));
 
   // Renaming happens in place, where the name is already shown, rather than in
@@ -304,7 +306,6 @@ void SpaceSwitcherView::ShowName(const std::u16string& name) {
     return;
   }
   hovered_name_->SetText(name);
-  hovered_name_->SetVisible(!name.empty());
 }
 
 void SpaceSwitcherView::BeginRename(const SpaceId& id) {
